  "id": "COMPOUND:35932 - PROTEIN:5778",
  "verbalization": "(+)-Caryolan-1-ol is implicated in the regulation of DO4 through multiple distinct pathways. The drug is shown to target HuT78, a cell line that is also a target of Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine, and subsequently of DO4. Similarly, (+)-Caryolan-1-ol acts on Hepatocyte, which is a target of 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide, which also targets DO4. Additionally, the drug targets SQ20B, a molecule that ultimately leads to DO4. These findings suggest that (+)-Caryolan-1-ol exerts its biological effects through different molecular mechanisms, all of which converge on DO4. The evidence supports a direct interaction between (+)-Caryolan-1-ol and DO4, with the drug acting as a modulator of cellular processes that are ultimately linked to DO4. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for (+)-Caryolan-1-ol to influence DO4 through various molecular mechanisms, underscoring its role in cellular regulation.",
